  If reset shows 1 crossing where base shows many, the reset removes the
  wrap and the walk becomes a usable update rule. Section (4) is the
  independent check: base's response should keep oscillating as k grows
  while reset's should settle, because channels contract and rotations do
  not. That is the same statement as (2) from a different direction.
